<mj-text mj-class="heading">Review a possible vulnerability in your package</mj-text>
<mj-text>Hi,</mj-text>
<mj-text>
  Someone reported a possible vulnerability in a package you maintain, and we at the Erlang Ecosystem Foundation (EEF) CNA are
  coordinating it. We opened a private case for it and invited you, so we can work on it together.
</mj-text>
<mj-text>
  The invite names your <%= @provider %> account <span class="handle"><%= @username %></span>.
  Sign in with that account to read the report. Already signed up with <%= @other_provider %>?
  <a href="<%= @account_url %>" style="color: #1670ad; font-weight: 600;">Link <%= @provider %> to that account</a>
  first.
</mj-text>
<mj-button href="<%= @sign_in_url %>">Sign in with <%= @provider %></mj-button>
<mj-text>
  If we don't hear from you within <strong><%= @response_days %> days</strong>, we may publish the
  CVE without a fix, so that people who depend on the package can protect themselves. If you need
  more time, just tell us. Our
  <a href="<%= @process_url %>" style="color: #1670ad; font-weight: 600;">Maintainer Process</a>
  walks through each step and its timelines.
</mj-text>
<mj-text>
  Until the CVE is out, please keep this private: no public issues, pull requests or commits
  about it, since those would tell attackers before users can upgrade.
</mj-text>
<mj-text padding="0">
  <span style="font-weight: 600;">The EEF CNA</span>
</mj-text>
